	(text_box "This project serves as a practice exercise in PCB design for a Linux Single-Board-Computer (SBC).\nIt's targeted to be installed in an industrial environment.\n\nThe SBC incorporates Bluetooth, Wi-Fi and Ethernet functionality to allow device control over the air/network.\n\nThe SBC also optionally includes an LCD screen and a matrix keypad for physical device control.\n\nA USB hub provides the SBC with four downstream USB devices.\n\nFor debugging, a JTAG connection and a virtual COM port via a USB-C port is provided.\n\nA micro-SD card interface is provided for booting the device using a Linux image."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 13.97 170.18 0)
		(size 283.21 80.01)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width -0.0001)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
